Here's the most relevant guidance I found in official URA sources:

Under Section 42 TPCA, where a taxpayer fails to pay tax or file returns after receiving notice:

1. An authorized URA officer, accompanied by Uganda Police officers, may enter the taxpayer's business premises and affix official revenue seals or padlocks;

2. The premises remain closed for up to fourteen (14) days;

3. Obstructing an officer or breaking URA seals constitutes a criminal offence punishable by heavy fines or imprisonment;

4. Premises are de-sealed only upon full payment of the tax debt or execution of an approved instalment payment agreement.

If you get stuck at any step, URA is happy to help: visit https://ura.go.ug, email services@ura.go.ug, call toll-free 0800 117 000 / 0800 217 000, or WhatsApp 0772 140 000.

Here's the most relevant guidance I found in official URA sources:

To pay motor vehicle registration fees and number plate fees in Uganda:

1. Generate a Payment Registration Number (PRN) on the URA web portal (ura.go.ug) under e-Services > Motor Vehicle Registration;

2. Take the PRN to any commercial bank or pay via mobile money / bank agent;

3. Once payment reflects, present the receipt and vehicle for inspection at URA Nakawa to receive the registration plates.
